<LegalLayout title="Data Processing Agreement" updated="2026-05-05">
  <p>
    This Data Processing Agreement (“DPA”) supplements the EdgeSecura
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and applies whenever EdgeSecura
    processes Personal Data on behalf of a Customer. Capitalized terms not
    defined here have the meaning given in the Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Roles</h2>
  <p>
    The Customer is the Controller of Customer Personal Data. EdgeSecura is the
    Processor and acts only on documented instructions from the Customer.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Subject matter and duration</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Subject matter:</strong> provision of the EdgeSecura service.</li>
    <li><strong>Duration:</strong> the term of the Order Form, plus any return or deletion period agreed therein.</li>
    <li><strong>Nature and purpose:</strong> management of external identities throughout their lifecycle.</li>
    <li><strong>Categories of data subject:</strong> contractors, partners, vendors, guests, and other non-employee identities of the Customer.</li>
    <li><strong>Categories of data:</strong> name, business contact details, employment status with sponsor, role memberships, audit events.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>
    The Customer authorizes EdgeSecura to engage the sub-processors listed at
    <a href="/subprocessors">edgesecura.com/subprocessors</a>. EdgeSecura will
    give 30 days’ prior notice of new sub-processors and the Customer may
    object on reasonable grounds.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Security measures</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Logical tenant isolation in the primary data store.</li>
    <li>Encryption in transit and at rest using industry-standard ciphers; customer-managed keys on Growth and above.</li>
    <li>Least-privilege access controls and quarterly access reviews of EdgeSecura personnel.</li>
    <li>Tamper-evident audit log of administrative actions.</li>
    <li>Annual third-party penetration testing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Where Personal Data is transferred outside the EEA, UK, or Switzerland to a
    jurisdiction without an adequacy decision, EdgeSecura relies on the
    Standard Contractual Clauses incorporated by reference into this DPA.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Personal Data Breach</h2>
  <p>
    EdgeSecura will notify the Customer without undue delay, and in any case
    within 72 hours, after becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach affecting
    Customer Personal Data.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Audit rights</h2>
  <p>
    The Customer may audit EdgeSecura’s compliance with this DPA up to once per
    year, with reasonable notice and during business hours, subject to
    confidentiality obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Return and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Upon termination, EdgeSecura will return or delete Customer Personal Data
    within 30 days, except as required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    EdgeSecura — Data Protection Officer<br />
    <a href="mailto:privacy@edgesecura.com">privacy@edgesecura.com</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
